{"name":"Hedgehog Cactus Yellow Green","hex":"#c4aa5e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hedgehog","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small mammal of the subfamily Erinaceinae,  characterized by their spiny back and often by the habit of rolling up into a ball when attacked, native to Afro-Eurasia.","Any of several spiny mammals, such as the porcupine, that are similar to the hedgehog."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make use of a hedgehog barricade as a defensive maneuver.","To array with spiky projections like the quills of a hedgehog."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hedgehog"},{"term":"cactus","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any member of the family Cactaceae, a family of flowering New World succulent plants suited to a hot, semi-desert climate.","Any succulent plant with a thick fleshy stem bearing spines but no leaves, such as euphorbs."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Non-functional, broken, exhausted, dead."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cactus"},{"term":"yellow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of sunflower petals and lemons; the color obtained by mixing green and red light, or by subtracting blue from white light; the color evoked by light of wavelength around 580 nm; one of the three primary colors in subtractive color systems.","The middle light in a set of three traffic lights, the lighting of which indicates that drivers should stop short of the intersection if it is safe to do so."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a yellow hue.","Lacking courage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yellow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chartreuse (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Chartreuse is a color between yellow and green also referred to as yellow-green or greenish yellow. It was named because of its resemblance to the French liqueur green chartreuse, introduced in 1764. Similarly, chartreuse yellow is a yellow color mixed with a small amount of green, named after the drink yellow chartreuse. The wavelength and frequency of chartreuse is near 547.5 nm or 547.5 THz."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/RAF-Cardington-Shed02_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-RAF-Cardington-Shed02_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chartreuse_(color)","wikidata":"Q1153119"},{"title":"Shades of chartreuse","blocks":[{"text":"Shades of chartreuse are listed below. Chartreuse is a color between yellow and green, so named because of its resemblance to the color of the French liqueur green chartreuse."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Shades_of_chartreuse_%28x25%29.svg/330px-Shades_of_chartreuse_%28x25%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_chartreuse","wikidata":"Q105563495"},{"title":"Hedgehog cactus","blocks":[{"text":"Hedgehog cactus may refer to:"},{"items":["Pediocactus, a genus of cacti containing 6-11 species","Echinocereus, a genus of ribbed, usually small to medium-sized cylindrical cacti, comprising about 70 species from the southern United States and Mexico in very sunny rocky places","Echinopsis, a large genus of cacti native to South America containing 128 species"]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hedgehog_cactus","wikidata":"Q5697290"},{"title":"Hedgehog","blocks":[{"text":"A  hedgehog  is a spiny mammal of the subfamily Erinaceinae, in the eulipotyphlan family Erinaceidae. There are 17 species of hedgehog in five genera found throughout parts of Europe, Asia, and Africa, and in New Zealand by introduction. There are no hedgehogs native to Australia and no living species native to the Americas. However, the extinct genus Amphechinus was once present in North America."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Igel.JPG/330px-Igel.JPG?utm_sour